{{also|Knee}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|kne}}, from {{inh|en|ang|cnēow}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*kneu}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*knewą}}, from {{inh|en|ine-pro||*ǵnéw-o-m}}, a thematic derivative of {{m|ine-pro|*ǵónu}}.

See also {{cog|fy|knibbel}}, {{cog|nds|Knee}}, {{m|nds|Knie}}, {{cog|nl|knie}}, {{cog|de|Knie}}, {{cog|da|knæ}}, {{cog|no|kne}}, {{cog|sv|knä}}; also {{cog|hit|𒄀𒉡|tr=genu}}, {{cog|la|genū}}, {{cog|xto|kanweṃ|pos=dual}}, {{cog|txb|keni|kenī}}, {{cog|grc|γόνυ|t=knee}}, {{m|grc|γωνία|t=corner, angle}}, {{cog|cy|glin||knee}}, {{cog|xcl|ծունր}}, {{cog|ae|𐬲𐬥𐬎𐬨}}, {{cog|sa|जानु|tr=jā́nu}}.

The obsolete plural ''[[kneen]]'' is from {{inh|en|enm|kneen}}, {{m|enm|knen}}, {{m|enm|kneon}}, {{m|enm|kneuwene}}.

